{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Soft.</b> For she thought she would fall to the lot of Esau, and she wept — for everyone was saying: two sons to Rebekah and two daughters to Lavan, the elder for the elder and the younger for the younger (Bava Batra 123)." "<b>Form.</b> That is the shape of the face — as in ״יְתָאֲרֵהוּ בַשֶּׂרֶד״ (Isaiah 44:13); קונ\"פאש בְּלַעַ\"ז." "<b>Appearance.</b> That is the glow of countenance."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French contrefais, 'to portray/depict' (i.e., outline a face)"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:06.536387731Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}